{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work","id":196132,"title":"Do you think an Owod anime could work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-13T01:33:00-07:00","id":196132,"title":"Do you think an Owod anime could work?","content":"Would you like to see one?<br /> <br /> Also, what anime feels the closest to WoD in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:06:16-07:00","id":196177,"title":"","content":"Closest I could think of is Supernatural the Anime Series.<br /> <br /> I would like to see a WoD anime. But main problem would be they'll focus on Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T04:07:17-07:00","id":196179,"title":"","content":"I would pay for Mage oriented animu, enough said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:23:22-07:00","id":196264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=196177#post196177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a WoD anime. But main problem would be they'll focus on Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if they did at least it couldn't have been worse than Kindred: the Embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T07:45:16-07:00","id":196274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=196264#post196264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if they did at least it couldn't have been worse than Kindred: the Embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a challenge, but I'm sure it could be done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T09:22:18-07:00","id":196336,"title":"","content":"I can see it now.<br /> <br /> Jan Pieterzoon - &quot;Theo Bell-kun, call upon the Horn of Truth to summon Mecha Caine! The Techno-Wizard is too powerful to fight alone.&quot;<br /> Theo Bell - &quot;Yes Pieterzoon-san! By the power of Brujah, I summon MECHAAAA CAAAAINE!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T13:20:29-07:00","id":196535,"title":"","content":"Personally, i think it depends on who handles it. <br /> We know some studios might go all FUBAR on the proyect, some others might go right away for it. im not a huge anime fan but if i had to pick a crew for a show, i would pick<br /> The guys from Monster + The Guys from Lain + The Guys from Cowboy bebop and Yokko Kanno and the Seatbelts. even some of the writters and or composers from Death Note.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T15:00:40-07:00","id":196584,"title":"","content":"Im on the opinion that japan has subject it cannot (or rarely) do well in anime.<br /> <br /> Medieval fantasy: Either they just &quot;japanesse it&quot; (people eating japanasse food or using japanesse weapons when the setting is european) or they the play it meh with timeline. Its a sword and sorcery anime but the main protagonist is dressed like a comic book character from the 90s.<br /> <br /> And Werewolfs: Always with the damm dog ears, i have seeing just one manga who did well in a way &quot;wolf guy&quot; whose art was alright although the plot was hentai.<br /> <br /> I dislike the lack of investigations most anime suffer from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T16:12:36-07:00","id":196601,"title":"","content":"<i>Hunter: the Reckoning</i> already feels very anime to me. So could a pulpier take on <i>Orpheus</i>. Not advocating for either, but you asked.<br /> <br /> <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i> has always felt like a Saturday morning cartoon with gore heaped on top, kinda like a bloodier TMNT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T17:04:15-07:00","id":196607,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think a CWOD animation series would work. For W:tA, let it be about a bunch of Garou cubs doing their Rite of Passage and learning as they go. You pretty much have to make the series about a bunch of newbies since people that are not knowledgeable about the CWOD don't get totally lost watching it (<i>While adding some clever hints and references to the people that know the gameline</i>).<br /> <br /> If were are going for Japanese animation series that is some what close to one of the game lines:<br /> Ginga Nagareboshi Gin = Werewolf: the Apocalypse. A bunch of Garou get together to take down a Wyrm corrupt Gurahl.<br /> Wolf's Rain = Werewolf: the Apocalypse. After the Apocalypse.<br /> <a href=\"http://werewolf-news.com/2014/01/what-you-need-to-know-about-guardians-of-luna/\" target=\"_blank\">Guardians of Luna = I still don't know if this ever came out or not...</a><br /> <br /> <b>@atamajakki:</b> Did you know that TMNT was supposed to have a spin-off cartoon based on the mini-series Archie comics put out, <a href=\"http://tmntentity.blogspot.com/2011/06/mighty-mutanimals-cartoon-that-almost.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Mighty Mutanimals?</a> So basically, Changing Breeds: the series.<br /> <br /> I'm also surprised no one has brought up Attack on Titan yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 07-13-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4