ow for sure it was the 90s <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T08:18:23-07:00","id":196794,"title":"","content":"Uzumaki. You know how Garou use spirals as a symbol for the enemy? Here's a good illustration of how to make it very literal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T12:14:58-07:00","id":197079,"title":"","content":"Psycho Pass basically already is a Technocracy cartoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/79-alexisvalarr","name":"alexisvalarr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar79_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:06:43-07:00","id":197119,"title":"","content":"If they do make an Anime, would making Kuei-jin be more interesting.. anime-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T15:29:26-07:00","id":197233,"title":"","content":"For a general World of Darkness feel, the &quot;Nasuverse&quot; (Fate/Stay Night, Tsukihime and Kara no Kyoukai) is probably the closest thing I can think of. <br /> <br /> I don't know how well an anime World of Darkness would do; you'd have to focus it on one gameline. Hopefully not Vampire. For a show, I think Mage or Werewolf would work best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T19:20:21-07:00","id":197325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=196584#post196584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im on the opinion that japan has subject it cannot (or rarely) do well in anime. Medieval fantasy: Either they just &amp;quot;japanesse it&amp;quot; (people eating japanasse food or using japanesse weapons when the setting is european) or they the play it meh with timeline. Its a sword and sorcery anime but the main protagonist is dressed like a comic book character from the 90s. And Werewolfs: Always with the damm dog ears, i have seeing just one manga who did well in a way &amp;quot;wolf guy&amp;quot; whose art was alright although the plot was hentai. I dislike the lack of investigations most anime suffer from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> You really must not have watched much anime. Go watch Blood + or Ghost in the Shell or even Ergo Proxy. The protagonists are not always dressed up like ridiculous clowns waving around magic charms or forming machines in a fountain of cheesy effects. You want Non dog eared werewolves, watch Wolf's Rain. The anime Helsing does a good job with the setting in modern England without &quot;japanese-ing&quot; anything. (Though I may earn the scorn of all anime fans by saying this<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Watch Helsing DUBBED. All the characters are in England! They should fucking speak english! And the voice actors they got are pretty good. So... Score. <br /> <br /> I think if any medium could do the World of Darkness justice it could be Anime. A TV show is going to be limited by budget. Hence why so many shows with werewolves only show them as a partial transformation (Teen Wolf, Lost Girl, Buffy) or they make them just wolves (True Blood, Bitten, again Lost Girl) no Crinos werewolves, no studio has the budget for that and the technology to make it cost effective is still a ways off. But Anime has no such restrictions. It can be as serious, gory and as gritty as they can make it and there's quite a lot of anime out there that doesn't skimp on the blood and guts. (Attack on Titan, When the Cicadas Cry) so Anime might be able to get away with a lot more realism and dark subject matter than any cartoon, TV show or even Cable network can get away with in the rest of the world all without making it Japan-centric or resorting to sparkles and girls in school uniforms with huge improbable hair styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T21:03:23-07:00","id":197392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=197325#post197325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You really must not have watched much anime. Go watch Blood + or Ghost in the Shell or even Ergo Proxy. The protagonists are not always dressed up like ridiculous clowns waving around magic charms or forming machines in a fountain of cheesy effects. You want Non dog eared werewolves, watch Wolf's Rain. The anime Hellsing does a good job with the setting in modern England without &quot;japanese-ing&quot; anything. (Though I may earn the scorn of all anime fans by saying this<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Watch Hellsing DUBBED. All the characters are in England! They should fucking speak english! And the voice actors they got are pretty good. So... Score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually yes, i watched all those animes though Hellsing was dubbed in my country language. Problem is that anime has the emotional range of a air-horn. Its either furniture characters (like blood + haji) or like you said ridiculous clowns waving arround magic / overemotional people who just drag the plot endlessly in their inaction (Saya until she start wearing purple). And that's not even taking in account cultural things that just are alien to non-japanesse, like the weird mindset and reactions.<br /> <br /> Hellsing like you said is great example of a vampire anime done right. Its the perfect blend between japan animation + western setting (and even then, it had a werewolf with puppy ears) so long as you dont pay much attention to the setting because it wasn't ever explained (at least to my knowledge) about where all the being from the maga/ova came from and the status of the masquerade and why it seems that the hellsing organization relies only on Alucard to solve its problems. And for every hellsing or gunsmith cats whose setting match its location you have 100 animes in which is a totally western sword and fantasy history but people use katana and speaks about &quot;The spirit of their mighty blow&quot; or vampires are in truth an Egyptian race of alien or something like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=197325#post197325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if any medium could do the World of Darkness justice it could be Anime. A TV show is going to be limited by budget. Hence why so many shows with werewolves only show them as a partial transformation (Teen Wolf, Lost Girl, Buffy) or they make them just wolves (True Blood, Bitten, again Lost Girl) no Crinos werewolves, no studio has the budget for that and the technology to make it cost effective is still a ways off. But Anime has no such restrictions. It can be as serious, gory and as gritty as they can make it and there's quite a lot of anime out there that doesn't skimp on the blood and guts. (Attack on Titan, When the Cicadas Cry) so Anime might be able to get away with a lot more realism and dark subject matter than any cartoon, TV show or even Cable network can get away with in the rest of the world all without making it Japan-centric or resorting to sparkles and girls in school uniforms with huge improbable hair styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but remember also that anime is restricted in what plot it can have and in characters. Most animes (not counting ovas/movies) have the same tropes over and over just poping out. For all the praise attack on titan has its protagonist are dragged down by said character tropes that they are forced to wear (the rei ayanami, the hothead, etc). That is without taking in account the rampant laziness in proper investigation animes/manga show when its time to represent a place that's is not japan.<br /> <br /> Perfect example of what im saying is the anime shiki. Brutal anime about what would happen if a sabbat pack went bananas in a town. And all the drama of this people having to kill their love ones is somewhat ruined when you see the stupid haircut and hair color of the people in it. You have the normal people and you have this clowns who don't blend with neither the tone nor stetic of the anime who stick out like a sore thumb.<br /> <br /> See? <a href=\"http://chikiotaku.mx/wp-content/uploads/sites/11/2013/08/shiki21.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://chikiotaku.mx/wp-content/uplo...08/shiki21.png</a> Tell me if the pink pig-tailed girl isn't out of place<br /> <br /> The perfect blend would be a american studio doing the script and a japanesse one doing the animation and the japanesse studio should be keep on a tight leash about the art direction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":".  Found a perfect example of the sore thumb thing 07-15-2014, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T21:38:35-07:00","id":197464,"title":"","content":"Guys, what about Tokyo ghoul?<br /> <br /> I heard about that show around. If you put Tokyo Ghoul in WOD concept, would they be like Kuei Jin?<br /> <br /> For anyone here that watched it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T00:17:56-07:00","id":197639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=197392#post197392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The perfect blend would be a american studio doing the script and a japanesse one doing the animation and the japanesse studio should be keep on a tight leash about the art direction</div> </div> </div> </div>So something like the Boondocks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T08:22:03-07:00","id":197937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=197392#post197392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hellsing like you said is great example of a vampire anime done right. Its the perfect blend between japan animation + western setting (and even then, it had a werewolf with puppy ears)</div> </div> </div> </div>Schrodinger was a werewolf only in the sense that there was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werwolf\" target=\"_blank\">a historical military unit in Nazi Germany known as the Werwolf</a>, and that the manga kept the name as the designation for the fictional forces displayed therein. Schrodinger himself is, as his name and ears would suggest, a Schrodinger's catboy. You can't be sure if he's alive or dead or where he is. He's noted as self-observing, however, so he can easily reset himself into different locations and come back to life if observed as dead. &quot;Looks like that catboy was self-cleaning. and/or magical.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only actual werewolf in the sense of the monster type is The Captain. He does not partake of the moe as Schrodinger does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T09:46:43-07:00","id":197996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=197937#post197937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Schrodinger was a werewolf only in the sense that there was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werwolf\" target=\"_blank\">a historical military unit in Nazi Germany known as the Werwolf</a>, and that the manga kept the name as the designation for the fictional forces displayed therein. Schrodinger himself is, as his name and ears would suggest, a Schrodinger's catboy. You can't be sure if he's alive or dead or where he is. He's noted as self-observing, however, so he can easily reset himself into different locations and come back to life if observed as dead. &quot;Looks like that catboy was self-cleaning. and/or magical.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only actual werewolf in the sense of the monster type is The Captain. He does not partake of the moe as Schrodinger does.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct my manga edtion in spanish reffers to him as a Werewolf like the myth not the military unit. My bad.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:36:08-07:00","id":198751,"title":"","content":"You know, perfect adaptation of Mage Ascension would be if people who are fans of Jojo's Bizarre Adventure and/or HunterxHunter got to adapt it. Those settings run on crazy, creative and complicated powers that still make sense within the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:34:55-07:00","id":198985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/196132-do-you-think-an-owod-anime-could-work?p=198751#post198751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, perfect adaptation of Mage Ascension would be if people who are fans of Jojo's Bizarre Adventure and/or HunterxHunter got to adapt it. Those settings run on crazy, creative and complicated powers that still make sense within the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, other than King Crimson, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07