nts":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T10:01:44-07:00","id":945514,"title":"","content":"Didn't look at the date, I figured someone might Google it and find it like me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:02:09-07:00","id":946492,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see one for each of the main splats all in the same universe with possible spin offs or cameos for the other splats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:10:13-07:00","id":946851,"title":"","content":"Make a horribly overpowered vampire with max dots in Celerity, Fortitude and Potence, then have him one-shot everything he fights. It's like One Punch Man but with vampires, fighting agasint a varity of non-werewolf Breeds and Fomori.<br /> <br /> Mage could also work with its bizarre magic, with Horizon being the main base of operations. Or maybe even Changeling and its unusual trappings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:34:36-07:00","id":946859,"title":"","content":"I think it could work, but definitely would be tricky, and would need careful composition.<br /> <br /> It would definitely need the..maturity of something like GiTS, Darker Than Black or Witch Hunter Robin. Anime can quickly fall into a tone that just doesn't suit the WoD well, either through quirkyness or simply over-the-topness that isn't played in a serious enough manner.<br /> <br /> That said, certain archetypical styles of storytelling that can be found in some anime *can* work quite well for WoD, A certain tame start, character buildup, raising of stakes, plot twists, and an epic finale.<br /> <br /> There are other types of anime arcs that also lend themselves well to more calm, personal stories that are centric on simply a single character or small set of characters. Changeling and Mage would benefit of something like that, though Mage also works for the more dramatic angle.<br /> <br /> All in all - yes, it can work. Just be careful with the anime-ish tropes, and cherrypick the really good parts of that media genre.<br /> More GiTS, Witch Hunter Robin, Shiki, Another, Gungrave or Noein (with the annoying tropes cut out) and Kara no Kyoukai, and less Tokyo Ghoul, DMC and Bleach-like fests.<br /> <br /> Heck, titles like Paprika or The Girl Who Leapt Through Time can be quite WoDish despite the lighter tones, especially when going for Changeling or Mage, so..yes. It can work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"